{
  "_comment": [
    "Golden frames for BRIDGE_PROTOCOL.md (§7 testing contract). THE shared",
    "location: the Python suite (tests/test_bridge_protocol_frames.py) and the",
    "TypeScript node (bridge-node/test/, which copies this directory into its",
    "build) both assert against this one file. A frame change that only updates",
    "one side fails that side's suite. Supersedes bridge-node/test/fixtures/e0-frames.json.",
    "",
    "Shapes only — bridgeVersion/matterJsVersion are substituted at assert time,",
    "since they track package.json and the pinned matter.js release.",
    "",
    "Top level: the handshake, every exchange the node implements, and every §5",
    "event. 'pending' is the holding pen for commands the node does not implement",
    "yet — the TS suite skips those, the Python client suite does not — and since",
    "E5 it is EMPTY: every frame here is answered by a real handler on both sides.",
    "",
    "E4 graduated 'attach_all_roles' and the whole 'set_state_*' family; E5",
    "graduated the last five, the fabric/reset/rebuild family (§3.9-§3.11) plus",
    "the endpoint_map_invalid refusal.",
    "",
    "Three frames are deliberately not what a live node produces from a cold start,",
    "and the suites know it:",
    " - 'attach' answers with an EMPTY endpoint set, because the request it",
    "   answers carries `endpoints: []`. That is the lawful §3.1 pair, and it is",
    "   also what a node with nothing live does — the mass-removal guard only",
    "   fires against a non-empty live set.",
    " - 'unknown_command' uses a name that is not in §3 at all. It used to use",
    "   upsert_endpoint 'because the node does not know it yet', which made the",
    "   fixture expire the moment the handler landed.",
    " - 'rebuild_endpoint_map' answers with endpoint numbers that differ from every",
    "   other status frame (4 and 5, not 2 and 3), because §3.11 exists precisely",
    "   for the case where the numbers moved and the user has accepted it. Its",
    "   driftChecked was 'false' while this frame was pending and is 'true' since",
    "   E5: §4.3's rule is 'false until the node persists the map', and a rebuild",
    "   persists one. drift is then empty because the map was just written FROM the",
    "   live set — trivially true, not an all-clear about anything that came before.",
    "",
    "'get_status' carries the same StatusReport 'attach_with_endpoints' returns:",
    "§6.2's invariant is that attach answers with exactly what get_status would,",
    "so the two frames sharing a payload is the contract, not a copy-paste.",
    "",
    "'command_unexported_device' targets an indigoDeviceId in no endpoint set, for",
    "the path where the allow-list no longer contains the device an ecosystem just",
    "acted on (§5 / PRD §7 race row): no action, one warning."
  ],
